Here is a clean, self-contained checklist of everything you need to download, where to get it, and the exact step-by-step order of operations to unlock and root your Moto G Play (2026) Cricket (XT2615-2, codename nevada, build W1WN36.18-111-7-2) on Windows 11.

Phase 1: Downloads (Save Everything to One Folder, e.g., C:\MotoRoot\)

1. Stock Firmware (W1WN36.18-111-7-2 — Cricket XT2615-2 / nevada)
	• Where to get it: Needrom — Moto G Play 2026 XT2615-2 CRICKET or Lolinet Motorola Mirrors (lenomola) (check under nevada -> CRICKET).
	• What to extract: Open the .zip and pull out only these three files into C:\MotoRoot\:
		• lk.img
		• init_boot.img
		• vbmeta.img
2. Android SDK Platform-Tools (adb & fastboot)
	• Where to get it: Android Developer Platform-Tools
	• What to extract: Unzip platform-tools directly into C:\MotoRoot\platform-tools\.
3. Motorola USB Drivers (for Windows 11 Fastboot)
	• Where to get it: Motorola Official USB Drivers
	• Setup: Run the installer on Windows 11.
4. Python 3 (for Windows 11)
	• Where to get it: Python.org Windows Downloads
	• Setup: During installation, check the box "Add python.exe to PATH".
5. Bootloader Exploit Tool (val-protocol / Valhalla)
	• Where to get it: Maikyxd/val-protocol on GitHub (and optionally crabcakes97/Valhalla on GitHub).
	• Setup: Click Code -> Download ZIP, extract into C:\MotoRoot\val-protocol\, and copy your extracted lk.img into that same folder.
6. Official Magisk App (.apk)
	• Where to get it: topjohnwu/Magisk Releases on GitHub
	• Setup: Download the latest Magisk-vXX.X.apk to C:\MotoRoot\.

Phase 2: Unlock the Bootloader

1. Boot Phone Into Fastboot Mode:
	• Power the Moto G Play completely off.
	• Hold Volume Down + Power until the black AP Fastboot Flash Mode screen appears, then plug it into your Windows 11 laptop via USB.
2. Verify Connection & Get Serial Number:
	• Open Command Prompt inside C:\MotoRoot\platform-tools\ and run:cmd
fastboot devices
Use code with caution.
	• Note the serial number printed next to fastboot.
3. Patch lk.img and Generate Unlock Key:
	• Open Command Prompt inside C:\MotoRoot\val-protocol\ and run the lk_auto_patch.py script against your lk.img (follow the exact syntax printed in the repo's README, supplying your phone's serial number when prompted).
	• This outputs a patched lk image (e.g., lk_patched.img) and your device's 20-character unlock key.
4. Flash Patched lk.img & Unlock:
	• From C:\MotoRoot\platform-tools\, flash the patched lk.img to your active slot (_a or _b—check with fastboot getvar current-slot), reboot back into Fastboot, and run the unlock command:cmd
fastboot flash lk_a lk_patched.img
fastboot reboot bootloader
fastboot oem unlock YOUR_GENERATED_KEY
Use code with caution.
	• Use the Volume buttons on the phone to confirm unlocking. The phone will wipe all user data and reboot.

Phase 3: Root With Magisk

1. Initial Offline Setup:
	• Complete the first-time Android setup screen offline (skip Wi-Fi and Google sign-in so com.motorola.paks cannot pull carrier updates).
2. Patch init_boot.img on the Phone:
	• Plug the phone into your PC (set USB mode to File Transfer) and copy Magisk-vXX.X.apk and your untouched stock init_boot.img to the phone's Download folder.
	• On the phone, open the Files app, install Magisk-vXX.X.apk, open Magisk, tap Install -> Select and Patch a File, and pick init_boot.img.
	• Copy the newly created magisk_patched-XXXXX.img from the phone's Download folder back into C:\MotoRoot\platform-tools\ on your laptop.
3. Flash vbmeta and Magisk init_boot:
	• Copy your untouched stock vbmeta.img into C:\MotoRoot\platform-tools\.
	• Power off the phone, hold Volume Down + Power to re-enter Fastboot Mode, connect to your laptop, and run:cmd
fastboot --disable-verity --disable-verification flash vbmeta_a vbmeta.img
fastboot --disable-verity --disable-verification flash vbmeta_b vbmeta.img
fastboot flash init_boot_a magisk_patched-XXXXX.img
fastboot reboot
Use code with caution.
4. Final Verification & Debloat:
	• Once booted, open the Magisk app—it will show Installed: XX.X and prompt for one final reboot to finish environment setup.
	• With root active, you can permanently freeze or remove com.motorola.paks before connecting to Wi-Fi.
